From: OHOS wine port
Subject: [PATCH] meson: make libatomic lookup optional for llvm-mingw x86

libatomic is a GCC-specific shim library; when building the 32-bit x86
target with the llvm-mingw toolchain, the compiler-rt builtins
(libclang_rt.builtins) already provide the __atomic_*_8 entry points and
no libatomic.a exists in the i686 sysroot. Make the lookup optional so
the build falls back to the compiler-provided atomics instead of
aborting during meson setup.
---
 meson.build | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -135,8 +135,11 @@
 
   # Need to link against libatomic for 64-bit atomic emulation on x86
-  # when using clang.
+  # when using GCC-style toolchains. The llvm-mingw compiler-rt builtins
+  # already provide the __atomic_*_8 symbols, so the lookup is optional.
   if vkd3d_is_clang
-    lib_atomic = vkd3d_compiler.find_library('atomic')
-    vkd3d_extra_libs += lib_atomic
+    lib_atomic = vkd3d_compiler.find_library('atomic', required: false)
+    if lib_atomic.found()
+      vkd3d_extra_libs += lib_atomic
+    endif
   endif
 endif
-- 
